[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: UAOP software high-level requirements
UID: UAOP-HLR-SET
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-21
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: ../02-standards/requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Behaviour of each software item at its interfaces. Active requirements are written from the code and tests as read on 2026-11-21 and are in the present tense; Proposed requirements are for items or behaviour not built. Each has one system requirement as parent (`docs/lifecycle/03-system/system-requirements.sdoc`) and a verification method. VERIFICATION_NOTE names the existing test file where one was seen; tests do not yet carry requirement tags.

These ids (`HLR-<AREA>-nnn`) are a different series from the product requirements `UAOP-HLR-nnn` (see `docs/lifecycle/02-standards/requirements-standard.md`, section 1).
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: API gateway (GW)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-001
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /vehicles/{id}/commands` maps the command name (ARM, DISARM, MODE, RTL, TAKEOFF, LAND, MISSION_START) to its `CommandKind`, calls `SubmitCommand` for the vehicle in the path, and answers 202 with the correlation identifier.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/grpc-forwarding.test.js`
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-002
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
A command name outside the set is refused with 400 and code `ERROR_CODE_INVALID_ARGUMENT`, and no service call is made.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/grpc-forwarding.test.js`
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-003
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
When the service call fails the gateway answers 502 with code `ERROR_CODE_UNAVAILABLE`; it never reports a command as accepted or rejected itself.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: No test of the failure branch was seen.
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-004
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /commands/{correlationId}` returns the `CommandResult` given by `GetCommandResult`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/grpc-forwarding.test.js`
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-005
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The gateway passes the `Idempotency-Key` request header to the service as `idempotency_key`, empty when absent.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: Does less than SYS-011 asks: a missing key is not refused (PR-010).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-006
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The command routes answer 401 unless the request carries a bearer token that verifies (HS256), has not expired and is not on the revoked list.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/jwt-auth.test.js` covers the token and the list; no test of the middleware on a route was seen.
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-007
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
Logout puts the token's identifier on the revoked list for the rest of the token's life.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: The revoked list is built and tested. The logout route as wired cannot reach it (PR-015).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-008
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
On a `subscribe` message at `/ws/v1` the gateway relays each bus message on the requested telemetry and event subjects as a frame with the stream name, a sequence number counting from 1 per stream, a time and the payload in base64, and relays nothing from subjects not requested.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/websocket-streams.test.js`
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-009
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
For a telemetry stream with `rate_hz` set, the gateway relays at most that many frames per second and reports the number of messages it dropped in a `gap` frame sent before the next relayed frame.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: `backend/api-gateway/tests/websocket-streams.test.js`
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-010
STATUS: Active
STATEMENT: >>>
The gateway sends a `heartbeat` frame on every open connection at the configured interval, 5 s by default.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
VERIFICATION_NOTE: No test was seen.
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-011
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The command routes shall answer 403 unless the token's role may command, and shall pass the actor's identity and role to the service with the call.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: PR-005.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-012
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The WebSocket shall refuse a connection without a valid token and shall refuse a subscription whose vehicle, category or domain is not a plain identifier the session may read.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: PR-004.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-GW-013
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
Each relayed frame shall carry the source time of the message unchanged, separate from the gateway's own send time.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: PR-006.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

