[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Vehicle link (LNK), planned

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-LNK-001
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle link shall decode MAVLink v2 from PX4 and ArduPilot into the telemetry contract, publish each category on its subject with source time and per-source sequence, and count and drop frames it cannot decode.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-LNK-002
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle link shall publish a link-lost event when no heartbeat has arrived for 3 s and a link-restored event on the next heartbeat.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link
COMMENT: The timeout logic of `tools/service-template/src/domain/link_monitor.h` is the starting point (PR-012).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-LNK-003
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle link shall send each admitted command to the one target vehicle, track its acknowledgement with bounded retries, and report accepted, rejected with the autopilot's reason, or timed out.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Vehicle manager (VM), planned

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VM-001
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle manager shall admit a command only from the session holding controlling authority for the vehicle, or an emergency-class command from any authenticated pilot session, and shall reject all others with a reason.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-manager
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VM-002
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle manager shall publish a command to the vehicle link only after its audit event is acknowledged as stored, and shall write an emergency-class command to a local log when the store is unavailable.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-manager
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VM-003
STATUS: Proposed
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle manager shall refuse a submission without an idempotency key and shall answer a repeated key with the original correlation identifier without publishing the command again.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-manager
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

